. In the first three models, the approach to data generation is to make use of some &lt;em&gt;noise space&lt;/em&gt;, denoted as $\mathcal{Z}$. A mapping from the noise space to data space is learned, using training data and various training methods. To obtain a sample from the generative model, one first samples a noise vector $z$ from the noise space $\mathcal{Z}$, and then inputs the noise vector to the learned mapping, and obtains generated sample from the model output. Note that for many common distributions like Gaussian, samples can be generated as transformation of noises.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
